Cold Mailbot - Overall Workflow (Code-Accurate)

Last verified from code:
- src/server.js
- src/services/campaignStorage.js
- src/services/websiteFetchService.js
- src/services/chromeProfileFetchService.js
- src/services/mailerDocService.js
- src/services/campaignSendService.js
- src/services/mailerSendService.js
- public/app.js

==================================================
1) What this system does
==================================================
Cold Mailbot is a local Node.js app that runs a full outbound pipeline:
1. Ingest campaign spreadsheet rows.
2. Fetch website context per row.
3. Generate structured mailer fields with Ollama.
4. Generate email preview (subject + body) with Ollama.
5. Let user send emails row-by-row or in bulk.
6. Persist every stage back to enriched Excel + metadata JSON + send logs.

It also supports a standalone single-lead mailer mode (/api/content/* routes).

==================================================
2) Main runtime components and what each uses
==================================================
Backend:
- Express server: src/server.js
- Validation: zod schemas in src/schemas/contentSchemas.js

AI generation:
- Ollama HTTP API /api/generate via src/services/ollamaClient.js
- Prompt templates in src/prompts/contentPrompts.js
- Draft/subject rules in src/utils/contentRules.js

Campaign orchestration and persistence:
- src/services/campaignStorage.js
- Spreadsheet read/write: xlsx
- Storage root: storage/campaigns/<campaignId>/

Website fetching:
- src/services/websiteFetchService.js
- Primary active fetcher: fetchViaRealChromeProfile() in src/services/chromeProfileFetchService.js
- Browser automation: Playwright Chromium persistent context

Mailer field document:
- src/services/mailerDocService.js
- DOCX creation library: docx

Email preview + send:
- src/services/campaignSendService.js
- src/services/mailerSendService.js
- Delivery providers: Gmail SMTP (nodemailer) or Resend API

Frontend:
- public/app.js
- Calls backend routes and manages row actions, polling, SSE, bulk send delays

==================================================
3) Boot and service wiring flow
==================================================
On startup (src/server.js):
1. Load env config from src/config.js.
2. Create two Ollama clients:
   - content model (OLLAMA_MODEL)
   - mailer model (OLLAMA_MAILER_MODEL)
3. Construct services:
   - ContentService
   - CampaignStorage
   - MailerDocService
   - MailerSendService
   - CampaignSendService
4. Register campaign pipeline handlers into CampaignStorage:
   - buildMailerDoc -> MailerDocService.generateForCampaignRow
   - buildSendPreview -> CampaignSendService.buildPreviewForRow
   - onRunStart / onRunComplete -> model unload/warmup lifecycle
   - NOTE: sendPreparedEmail handler is NOT attached in current server wiring.
5. Verify mail transport if configured.
6. Serve static UI and API routes.

Model lifecycle detail:
- On run start: unload then warmup configured model(s).
- On final run completion/stopped/failed: unload model(s).

==================================================
4) Data model and statuses
==================================================
Campaign-level status values:
- running, paused, completed, stopped, failed

Row-level status values:
- queued
- fetching
- fetched
- generating_mail
- generating_preview
- awaiting_verification (reserved path exists)
- ready
- sent
- paused
- failed
- done (legacy normalized to ready)

Email status column values commonly used:
- pending
- preview_ready
- sent
- send_failed (manual send failure path)
- completed (set by /api/campaigns/mailer-doc route)

Destination columns persisted to enriched sheet:
- jina_content
- jina_error
- jina_fetch_method
- jina_sub_pages
- jina_fetch_trace
- linkedin_content
- linkedin_description
- linkedin_error
- email_status
- email_to
- email_subject
- email_generated_body
- email_body
- email_previewed_at
- email_sent_at
- email_message_id
- email_error

Storage artifacts per campaign folder:
- original upload file
- enriched file (<original-stem>-enriched.<ext>)
- metadata.json (+ metadata.json.bak)
- mailer-row-<row>.docx files
- send-row-<row>-<timestamp>.json files

==================================================
5) Campaign workflow: end-to-end
==================================================
A) Campaign creation (POST /api/campaigns)
1. UI reads file to base64 and sends { campaignFile, count }.
2. CampaignStorage.saveUpload():
   - validates extension (.xlsx/.xls/.csv)
   - writes original file to storage/campaigns/<campaignId>/
   - reads first worksheet rows
   - auto-detects website column (required)
   - detects email column (optional)
   - normalizes destination columns on rows
   - creates queueRows for first count rows (Excel rowNumber = index + 2)
   - writes enriched workbook
   - writes metadata.json with status=running
3. ensureRunProcessor(campaignId) is started immediately.

B) Run processor starts
1. processCampaignRows() loads metadata and checks target row count.
2. If rowConcurrency > 1, it enters concurrent pipeline:
   - fetch worker pool (claimNextFetchRow)
   - generation worker pool (claimNextGenerationRow)
3. If rowConcurrency == 1, it uses sequential path but same stage logic.

C) Fetch stage per row
1. Row claimed and status -> fetching.
2. Website fetch call:
   - enrichWebsiteContent(websiteUrl, options)
   - fetchWebsiteContent() currently calls only fetchViaRealChromeProfile()
3. Active fetch method behavior:
   - fetchMethod label: chrome_profile or chrome_profile_search_test (PROFILE_SEARCH_ONLY=true)
   - can run headless with optional headful fallback
   - can mirror default Chrome profile into automation directory
4. Fetched output:
   - cleaned text
   - internal links
   - fetch trace
5. Sub-page enrichment:
   - if SUBPAGE_FETCH_ENABLED=true and not profile-search-only
   - candidate internal links are selected
   - each subpage fetched through same fetchWebsiteContent path
   - combined into final content blocks
6. Persist fetch outputs into enriched row:
   - jina_content / jina_error / jina_fetch_method / jina_sub_pages / jina_fetch_trace
7. Protection handling:
   - Kasada or challenge-like warnings mark fetch as blocked/protected
   - protected rows are set failed and skip mail generation

D) Mailer doc stage per row
1. Row status -> generating_mail.
2. Handler calls MailerDocService.generateForCampaignRow().
3. MailerDocService:
   - prompts mailer Ollama model to return structured JSON fields
   - robust JSON extraction and fallback normalization
   - infers missing company/context values from source row/URL
   - writes DOCX file mailer-row-<row>.docx
4. Row metadata gets mailerFields and docFileName.

E) Preview generation stage per row
1. Row status -> generating_preview.
2. Handler calls CampaignSendService.buildPreviewForRow().
3. Preview flow:
   - resolve recipient email from explicit value or source row columns
   - reuse existing mailer fields if present, else build via mailer service
   - generate content (combined mode preferred if enabled)
   - fallback to split draft + subject generation
   - fallback again to deterministic draft/subject templates when needed
   - wrap final preview body with greeting + signature
4. Persist preview fields:
   - email_to
   - email_subject
   - email_generated_body
   - email_body
   - email_previewed_at
   - email_status=preview_ready

F) Optional auto-send stage in pipeline
- CampaignStorage has a sendPreparedEmail stage hook, but server currently does not set this hook.
- Result: campaign run auto-generates previews, but does not auto-send by default.

G) Row finalization
- If preview generated and not sent: status -> ready
- If sent: status -> sent
- Duration/error fields updated.

H) Campaign finalization
- When no pending rows:
  - campaign status -> completed
  - completedAt set

==================================================
6) Website fetch internals (current active path)
==================================================
fetchViaRealChromeProfile() details:
1. Resolve Chrome executable and user-data/profile.
2. Launch persistent context.
3. Two operating modes:
   - profileSearchOnly=true:
     - open Google search for target URL
     - open first organic result
     - hard refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R equivalent + CDP ignore cache)
     - close popups/cookie banners
     - random human-like scroll
     - capture homepage text
     - optionally open About and Services links and capture text
     - return combined snapshot text with source=chrome_profile_search_test
   - profileSearchOnly=false:
     - navigate directly to target URL (with alternate www/non-www retry)
     - wait, handle cookie UI and popups
     - auto-scroll and extract body text + internal links
     - reject blocked/challenge/too-short content
     - return cleaned text with source=chrome_profile
4. On finish, close context.

Important current behavior:
- Manual verification UI plumbing exists at API/UI level, but current chrome fetch path logs and continues with "manual verification flow disabled" and does not emit verification events.

==================================================
7) Manual row actions in UI (after fetch/generation)
==================================================
Row generate preview action (public/app.js rowGenerate):
1. POST /api/campaigns/mailer-doc
2. POST /api/campaigns/send-preview
3. Cache preview state in UI for inline editing

Row send action (public/app.js rowSend):
1. POST /api/campaigns/send with to/subject/body/mailerFields
2. Backend CampaignSendService.sendPreparedEmail() calls MailerSendService.sendColdEmail()
3. On success, backend updates row:
   - email_sent_at, email_message_id, email_status=sent
4. On failure, backend sets:
   - email_status=send_failed, email_error=<reason>

Bulk send action (public/app.js sendAllReadyRows):
1. Collect send-ready rows (ready + preview exists + not already sent).
2. Send each row sequentially.
3. Wait random delay 1s to 10s between sends.
4. Track sent/failed counts in UI state.

==================================================
8) Mail provider send workflow
==================================================
MailerSendService provider selection:
1. If MAIL_PROVIDER=resend and RESEND_API_KEY + RESEND_FROM exist -> Resend.
2. Else if Gmail creds exist (GMAIL_USER + GMAIL_APP_PASS/GMAIL_PASS/APP_PASS) -> Gmail SMTP.
3. Else -> unconfigured.

Send path:
- validate to/subject/body
- optional send delay (MAILER_SEND_DELAY_MS)
- send via selected provider
- return message id and accepted/rejected list

==================================================
9) Control operations workflow
==================================================
Pause (POST /api/campaigns/:id/pause):
- campaign -> paused
- active row may move to paused
- pausedAtRow/resumeFromRow updated

Resume (POST /api/campaigns/:id/resume):
- campaign -> running
- paused/fetching/generating/awaiting_verification rows reset to queued
- ensureRunProcessor() starts again

Stop (POST /api/campaigns/:id/stop):
- campaign -> stopped
- stoppedAt + resumeFromRow set

Reset (POST /api/campaigns/:id/reset):
- requires campaign not running
- clears all enrichment + mail columns in enriched workbook
- rows reset to queued/pending state
- campaign status -> paused

Retry row (POST /api/campaigns/:id/rows/:rowNumber/retry):
- clears row website+email outputs
- sets row queued/pending
- campaign set running and processor resumes

Delete rows (POST /api/campaigns/:id/rows/delete):
- blocked while running
- rebuilds worksheet without deleted rows
- reindexes rowNumber (index+2)

==================================================
10) Standalone (non-campaign) content generation flow
==================================================
Routes:
- POST /api/content/draft
- POST /api/content/subject
- POST /api/content/generate
- POST /api/content/variants

Flow:
1. Validate lead payload with zod.
2. Build prompt from contentPrompts.js.
3. Call Ollama via OllamaClient streaming reader.
4. Normalize + compliance-check outputs via contentRules.js.
5. Return draft/subject/body/variants + compliance object.

==================================================
11) Notes on currently present but not active paths
==================================================
1. LinkedIn helper functions exist (query builders, description extraction), but active upload pipeline does not fetch LinkedIn content automatically.
2. websiteFetchService contains multiple helper fetch layers (Jina, Playwright, Google cache, chrome cookies), but fetchWebsiteContent currently uses mono Chrome profile fetch path.
3. CampaignStorage has sendPreparedEmail stage support, but server wiring currently leaves it null, so campaign run itself stops at preview-ready unless user sends manually.

==================================================
12) Practical end-to-end operator sequence
==================================================
1. Configure .env (Ollama + Chrome profile + mail provider).
2. Start app (npm run dev) and open UI.
3. Upload campaign sheet + row count.
4. Let pipeline fetch website context and auto-generate preview-ready rows.
5. Open row, review/edit preview.
6. Send per row or use Send All Ready.
7. Download enriched Excel and inspect per-row send JSON logs in storage/campaigns/<campaignId>/.
